CORE
zero_length_null.c
--pointer-check --bounds-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A zero-length __builtin_memcpy/__builtin_memmove with a null source or
destination is accepted (GCC/Clang builtin behaviour, C2y N3322).  Before the
fix: "memcpy source region readable: FAILURE".
